  "text": "The longest river in the world is the Nile River.\n\nTo understand herd immunity, think of it like a firewall in computer security. If enough computers (people) in a network are protected against a virus (infectious disease), it becomes very difficult for an infected computer (sick person) to spread that virus to other unprotected computers (people). The protection of the many creates a barrier that stops the spread, keeping the whole network safe."
